# Saha Plus Work Log

## Project

- Next.js 14 app in `src/app`.
- Start locally with `npm run dev`.

## Required change workflow

- After every completed code or documentation change, verify the result, commit it, and push it to `origin/main` before starting another change.
- Do not leave a completed change only in the local working tree; record the push result in this work log.

## Completed

### Login screen and interactive plus field

- Replaced the default Next.js starter page with a responsive Saha Plus sign-in screen.
- Added a green welcome panel filled with drifting plus signs.
- Plus signs respond to pointer movement, and pointer presses create a spreading ripple.
- Added reduced-motion handling and a compact mobile layout.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`.

### Plus field refinement

- Increased the field to 260 independently positioned plus signs.
- Added varied, continuous floating paths so the signs drift rather than sit on a grid.
- Plus signs grow as the pointer approaches and shift in response to pointer movement; pointer-down ripple remains.
- Kept the existing login layout and styling intact for this refinement.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`.

### Reference-matched particle field

- Matched the supplied recording's dense, evenly spaced particle field using 1,444 plus signs.
- Changed the welcome panel from green to deep blue.
- Plus signs softly blink and grow, brighten, and shift around the pointer.
- Kept the existing login layout and copy intact.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`.

### Particle performance and green palette

- Replaced 1,444 animated DOM nodes and pointer-driven React updates with a single canvas renderer.
- Capped rendering at roughly 30 FPS and device pixel ratio 1.5; pauses drawing while the tab is hidden.
- Preserved blinking and cursor-driven growth, brightness, and displacement.
- Changed the decorative panel and accents to a restrained green palette and simplified its background treatment.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`.

### Login form visual polish

- Refined form typography, spacing, input surfaces, and the primary action's hover and pressed states.
- Added explicit keyboard focus-visible styling and clearer link contrast.
- Left the green plus-sign panel, canvas, and animation unchanged.
- Files changed: `src/app/globals.css`.

### Wellness-focused login redesign

- Reworked the login-side welcome message and form hierarchy with warm sage surfaces and more distinctive wellness details.
- Added a compact privacy reassurance and refined the action area.
- Kept the green plus-sign panel, canvas, and animation unchanged.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`.

### In-place registration transition

- Added a registration form that replaces sign-in without navigating to a new page.
- Sign-in and registration forms crossfade in the same form area; the welcome/plus panel glides across with a brief damped sway, then settles.
- Added the reverse transition back to sign-in and reduced-motion handling.
- Preserved the plus canvas drawing implementation and symbol style.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`.

### Transition motion adjustment

- Kept the welcome panel stable in shape while it slides with a subtle blur.
- Moved the brief damped shake to the plus-sign canvas layer; it settles back to its resting position.
- Kept the plus rendering and styling unchanged.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`.

### Frontend quality pass

- Applied the bundled Geist font across the interface and tightened shared auth-form sizing, focus, and overflow behavior.
- Updated page title and description from the Next.js starter defaults.
- Left the plus canvas implementation and panel appearance unchanged.
- Files changed: `src/app/globals.css`, `src/app/layout.tsx`.

### Plus-field sweep and transition blur fix

- Added a repeating vertical light pulse that sweeps from edge to edge within the existing plus canvas.
- Changed the panel blur to a temporary transition animation that clears after switching in either direction.
- Kept the plus drawing and interaction behavior otherwise intact.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`.

### Horizontal ECG pulse

- Replaced the vertical scanning beam with a repeating, horizontally traveling ECG waveform drawn within the plus canvas.
- Shaped each beat with P, QRS, and T components and a restrained green glow.
- Kept the plus marks and transition behavior unchanged.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`.

### Live ECG trace and pre-database login destination

- Changed the ECG to draw progressively from a moving head, retaining only a short trail that fades behind it and resets at the panel edge.
- Added an in-app wellness home/menu screen reached on login form submission, regardless of entered credentials, until NeonDB authentication is connected.
- Added a sign-out action to return to the sign-in screen.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`.

### Collapsible navigation rail and scroll-story dashboard

- Replaced the full-width dashboard tab bar with a fixed left icon rail that expands to show tab names on hover or keyboard focus.
- Reframed the dashboard as a scroll story with three short chapters and a sticky anatomy-film placeholder ready for the generated video.
- Added responsive rail and story-stage layouts.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`.

### Scroll-scrubbed head-to-toe anatomy film

- Replaced the copy-led scroll chapters with a tall scroll track and a pinned portrait video frame; page scroll position now scrubs the video from its first frame to its last.
- Added a head-to-feet progress marker, a reduced-motion behavior that holds the opening frame, and a fallback until `public/media/anatomy-scroll.mp4` is supplied.
- Files changed: `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`.

### Generated anatomy recording integration

- Added the supplied Dreamina recording at `public/media/anatomy-scroll.mp4`, transcoded to H.264 Main/yuv420p with fast-start metadata (1248×704, 5 seconds, 863 KB).
- Matched the desktop player to the source's 39:22 aspect ratio and added a site-colored bottom-right UI panel over the watermark; mobile uses a centered portrait crop.
- The source shows the full male figure throughout rather than a head-to-toe camera pan, so scroll scrubs its available 5-second motion.
- Files changed: `public/media/anatomy-scroll.mp4`, `src/app/globals.css`, `init.readme`.

### Video playback compatibility fix

- Added a VP9/WebM source before the H.264/MP4 fallback, enabled eager media loading, and revealed the player on decoded data/can-play events.
- Added a distinct visible failure message if neither source loads.
- Verified the optimized build and confirmed the rebuilt local server returns `200 video/webm` and `200 video/mp4` with range support.
- Files changed: `public/media/anatomy-scroll.webm`, `src/app/page.tsx`, `init.readme`.

### Camera-driven 3D body atlas

- Matched the installed stack: React 18.3.1, Fiber 8.15.12, Drei 9.88.0, Three 0.160.0; added `@types/three` 0.160.0.
- Copied the supplied `male_body_base.glb` to `public/models/human.glb`, auto-fit it to 4 units tall with feet at y=0, and added the required Sketchfab/CC BY 4.0 attribution.
- Added a full-screen Three.js scene, eased vertical camera travel with a chest/core zoom, five alternating body-zone chapters, mobile bottom cards, progress navigation, lighting, fog, and a loading percentage.
- Dynamically imports the client-only scene. The model remains static while only the camera follows scroll.
- Files changed: `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `public/models/human.glb`, `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`, `src/components/BodyScene.tsx`, `init.readme`.

### Bounding-box camera keyframes, leg descent, and finale

- Replaced the camera interpolation with smooth keyframes whose head, chest, core, and foot targets are computed from the fitted model height (93%, 72%, 52%, and 3.5%). The close head framing uses a narrower FOV; after the head keyframe, camera distance only stays level or decreases.
- Held the chest framing at 4.7 units and the core/leg framing at 4.15 units, carrying the camera to the feet without a leg-section zoom out. Changed the final chapter to a FINALE card with dashboard and smooth back-to-top actions; there is no separate feet chapter.
- Added hemisphere and frontal fill lighting, studio environment lighting at 0.4 material environment intensity, a dimmed finale state, and no-shadow rendering. Removed the embedded JPEG normal map, kept vertex colors, enforced FrontSide materials, and computed normals only when absent.
- Added runtime mesh diagnostics and bounding-box landmark logs. The three named body meshes are retained; none was hidden because the GLB has no explicit redundant mesh naming and visual overlap cannot be established from its geometry metadata alone.
- Files changed: `src/components/BodyScene.tsx`, `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`, `init.readme`.

### Restore original GLB skin shading and horizontal drag rotation

- Kept the loaded GLB materials instead of replacing them. The source body color is carried by warm beige vertex colors, so the app enables those colors on the original materials; no fallback tint is needed. Color maps are marked sRGB when present. The JPEG normal map remains disabled from the prior shading repair.
- Added ACES filmic tone mapping at 0.9 exposure and toned down hemisphere, key, fill, environment, and green rim lighting. Light and exposure values are grouped in the scene config.
- Added horizontal-only pointer rotation with an invisible raycastable body hit area, axis locking so vertical touch gestures continue scrolling, damped motion, decaying inertia, cursor feedback, and shortest-path recentering after five idle seconds.
- Files changed: `src/components/BodyScene.tsx`, `init.readme`.

### Transparent anatomy scene, finale pull-back, and shared back-to-top control

- Removed the hit-area box from the rotating model and replaced it with a sibling vertical cylinder. It is raycastable but has opacity 0, color/depth writes disabled, depth testing disabled, and render order -1. The old Three.js ring is now a CSS ring behind the transparent Canvas.
- Made the Canvas alpha-transparent and removed the scene background color. Kept the dark green page background, while placing story HTML and UI layers above the Canvas.
- Added the post-legs camera return from feet at t=0.80 to the shared hero y/distance at t=0.98, then hold through t=1. The pull-back occupies the last scroll page; the finale card fades in near the restored full-body view and stays fixed through the end. The finale progress dot activates when the pull-back starts.
- Added an accessible floating Back to top pill, visible after the head section. It shares the finale card’s scroll-to-top action and resets model rotation to front-facing.
- Files changed: `src/components/BodyScene.tsx`, `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`, `init.readme`.

### Replace blank body base with a detailed, face-complete model

- Replaced `public/models/human.glb` with Innerscene’s CC0 male base mesh, adapted from MakeHuman. The model is a 109k-triangle rigged adult figure with sculpted eyes, ears, face, hands, and feet; its static A-pose fits the existing head-to-feet camera journey.
- Added `SkeletonUtils.clone` so the cloned skinned mesh retains its bone bindings. Retained the GLB’s original standard materials and normals, applying the site’s warm `#c9a58a` tone to its untextured neutral-gray clay material.
- Updated the visible source/license credit to the Innerscene/MakeHuman CC0 asset.
- Files changed: `public/models/human.glb`, `src/components/BodyScene.tsx`, `init.readme`.

